  "scalar_basis": "P=2pi, mu=m/P !=0; Phi_(m,r,n)=sqrt(P) exp(i mu z) sum_(k in Z) exp(i(r+k m)y) f_n(x+(r+k m)/mu), where f_n is the real unit-L2 Hermite function of frequency abs(mu). r=0,...,abs(m)-1. Haar measure is normalized by P^4.",
  "real_field": "conjugate(Phi_m,r,n)=Phi_-m,(-r mod abs(m)),n. Tensor conjugation also reverses spin. Use L=n+sign(m)*spin, invariant under this conjugation.",
  "closure_argument": "[iN,X]=-Y and [iN,Y]=X. The diagonal tensor action plus iN makes gradient, symmetrized gradient, divergence, curvature variation and ADM maps equivariant when g and pi have equal horizontal axes. All tensor spins are bounded, so a fixed L has finitely many slots. This grading is an algebraic operator on each Schrödinger representation, not a descended rotation isometry.",
  "boundary": "The displayed finite oscillator matrices are only a guard implementation. A second-order operator acting on n<=L+2 reaches at most L+4; retain that entire range before projecting. Never impose a finite-dimensional Heisenberg commutator at the guard edge.",
  "nonLRS_boundary": "If g1!=g2, the scalar operator contains nonzero n<->n+2 links for arbitrarily high n. The present finite grading no longer closes; this is not a theorem excluding every possible alternative basis."
